+## Statement
+
+Assume AC. Let $\Gamma\le\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb C)$ be discrete, torsion-free, nonelementary and geometrically finite. Let $D$ be a component of its ordinary domain, and $H=\operatorname{Stab}_\Gamma(D)$. Suppose the conformal boundary component $D/H\to(\mathbb H^3\cup\Omega_\Gamma)/\Gamma$ is fundamental-group injective. Suppose, additionally, that every parabolic element of $H$ acts parabolically in the disk uniformization of $D$.
+
+Then $H$ is geometrically finite, its limit set is a quasicircle, and $D$ and the opposite component $D^*$ of its sphere complement are quasidisks with one finite common quasidisk constant for this fixed model. Both are $H$-invariant. Their quotients are finite-type complete finite-area hyperbolic surfaces. Their punctures correspond bijectively by full primitive maximal-parabolic conjugacy classes, with the actual conjugating paths retained. There are no additional components of $\Omega_H$.
+
+The no-accidental-parabolic condition is not inferred from incompressibility alone. It follows, in particular, from the following ACTUAL realized pared marking data. Let $M$ be compact connected oriented, smooth or a GIVEN finite PL three-manifold, and $P$ a finite union of injective collared annuli and entire torus boundary components, with every torus boundary component included. Supply an isomorphism $\rho:\pi_1(M)\to\Gamma$ sending the peripheral subgroups to parabolics and accounting for every parabolic conjugacy class. Let $F$ be a component of $\partial M\setminus\operatorname{int}P$ with an actual boundary marking inducing an isomorphism $\pi_1(F)\to H$ equal to its inclusion followed by $\rho$. A componentwise homotopy equivalence in an incompressible realization supplies precisely this group datum. Suppose EVERY essential SIMPLE circle in $\operatorname{int}F$ homotopic through $M$ into $P$ is homotopic through $\partial M$ into $P$. Then the no-accidental condition above holds, and all the stated geometric conclusions follow. No all-loops version of that simple-circle condition is assumed. Both given categories and all peripheral tracks are retained. Elementary, empty-ordinary-domain and torus-boundary branches are not silently included in its negative-Euler-characteristic surface input. No initial hyperbolic representation or model for an original topological manifold is constructed here.
+
+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** The actual ambient GF group, its incompressible conformal boundary component, and the stated disk-action condition.
+
+[F1] Actual GF truncation gives a finite-type cofinite quotient and a simply connected lift for an incompressible conformal boundary. It also proves that this lift is a FULL component of $\Omega_H$. [[lem-standard-gf-truncations-give-finite-conformal-boundaries-and-cofinite-incompressible-uniformizers]]
+
+[F2] The invariant-domain theorem proves analytic finiteness, and under the given no-accidental hypothesis every other component is $H$-invariant and cofinite with exactly the same primitive peripheral classes. Its actual finite smooth-neighborhood/PL-annulus construction supplies simultaneous disjoint cylinders to any finite disjoint essential boundary circles. Finite collared cuts preserve the matched boundary-piece groups. [[thm-cofinite-invariant-ordinary-domains-have-finite-analytic-boundary]] [[lem-finite-annulus-cuts-preserve-isomorphic-boundary-piece-groups]]
+
+[F3] A cyclic frontier with surjective outside and nonhomotopic ordinary rims gives precisely two isolated primitive parabolic punctures, no third, and actual canonical mutually separated tubes with compact initial complements. [[lem-cyclic-frontier-annuli-pair-exactly-two-parabolic-punctures]]
+
+[F4] An actual peripheral circle bijection, group isomorphism and compatible conjugating paths give a relative PL surface homeomorphism realizing ALL those paths. An actual group isomorphism between closed negative-Euler-characteristic surfaces is likewise realized: construct an edge/relation map and apply the proved surface-map theorem, whose covering has degree one by group surjectivity. [[thm-peripherally-marked-surface-group-isomorphisms-have-relative-pl-homeomorphisms]] [[thm-pi-one-injective-finite-pl-surface-maps-are-covers-or-annular-collapses]]
+
+[F5] Compatible group and path data on a finite CW subpair extend to an actual map into a target with contractible universal cover, by edge assignments, relation disks and sphere fillings. The target need not be compact for this continuous conclusion. [[lem-peripherally-compatible-group-markings-have-relative-three-complex-maps]]
+
+[F6] Excision identifies local homology with the coordinate-ball orientation module; ball restrictions trivialize that module and compatible orientation classes restrict uniquely over compact supports. A finite oriented manifold triangulation has the orientation chain obtained by summing its oriented top simplices, with only its boundary faces remaining. [[lem-compatible-local-orientation-classes-exist-over-compact-subsets]] [[thm-excision-for-singular-homology]] [[thm-compact-smooth-manifolds-with-corners-admit-relative-finite-triangulations]]
+
+[F7] A type-preserving isomorphism between actual GF groups gives a continuous equivariant quasi-isometry of their convex hulls. A continuous plane-to-hull quasi-isometry gives a quasicircle with both complementary quasidisk bounds. [[lem-type-preserving-geometrically-finite-isomorphisms-give-convex-hull-quasi-isometries]] [[lem-convex-hulls-quasi-isometric-to-a-hyperbolic-plane-have-quasicircle-boundaries]] A sphere-loxodromic element cannot act parabolically on a simply connected ordinary domain, by the arbitrary-height strip estimate. [[lem-equivariant-univalent-strips-bound-loxodromic-log-multipliers]]
+
+[F8] The one-component parabolic root theorem applies to the actual simply connected $D$. Subgroup covers of the actual $M$ exist. In a given locally finite PL manifold with a group-isomorphic compact boundary core, the actual finite-neighborhood annulus construction retains a specified first rim, including in a noncompact cover. Smooth compact pairs have compatible finite whole-star triangulations. A loop homotopic THROUGH its boundary surface into annular paring is peripheral in its actual complementary surface component. [[lem-two-simply-connected-ordinary-components-have-root-closed-stabilizer-intersections]] [[thm-universal-cover-existence]] [[lem-subgroup-quotient-of-universal-cover]] [[lem-isomorphic-boundary-cores-carry-finite-disjoint-annulus-systems]] [[lem-compact-smooth-three-manifold-pairs-admit-compatible-whole-star-triangulations]] [[lem-boundary-surface-homotopies-into-annular-paring-are-peripheral]]
+
+[A1] Full choice is [[def-axiom-of-choice]].
